**Excerpt from Manufacturing Agreement**

**This Manufacturing Agreement (the “Agreement”) is made and entered into this 15th day of March, 2023, by and between:**

**1. XYZ Manufacturing Inc.**, a corporation organized and existing under the laws of the State of California, with its principal place of business located at 123 Industry Way, Los Angeles, California 90001 (hereinafter referred to as “Manufacturer”);

**2. ABC Corp.**, a corporation organized and existing under the laws of the State of New York, with its principal place of business located at 456 Commerce Blvd, New York, New York 10001 (hereinafter referred to as “Client”);

**RECITALS**

WHEREAS, the Client desires to engage the Manufacturer for the production of industrial equipment as detailed in Exhibit A (the “Products”); and

WHEREAS, the Manufacturer has the expertise, facilities, and personnel to manufacture the Products in accordance with the specifications provided by the Client.

NOW, THEREFORE, in consideration of the mutual covenants and agreements contained herein, the parties agree as follows:

**ARTICLE I: DEFINITIONS**

1.1 **“Production Line”** refers to the series of workstations and machinery at the Manufacturer’s facility located at 123 Industry Way, Los Angeles, California 90001, that will be utilized to manufacture the Products.

1.2 **“Quality Control”** (QC) refers to the systematic measurement, comparison with a standard, and monitoring of the manufacturing processes to ensure that the Products meet the quality standards established in Exhibit B.

1.3 **“Industrial Equipment”** refers to the machinery and tools used in the manufacturing process, including but not limited to the following: CNC machines, hydraulic presses, and assembly robots as detailed in Exhibit C.

**ARTICLE II: SCOPE OF WORK**

2.1 **Manufacturing Services**  
The Manufacturer shall manufacture the Products for the Client in accordance with the specifications set forth in Exhibit A. The Manufacturer shall ensure that the production lines operate at a capacity of no less than 80% efficiency per shift and aim to produce a minimum of 10,000 units per month.

2.2 **Quality Control Procedures**  
The Manufacturer shall implement rigorous Quality Control procedures as outlined in Exhibit B. This includes, but is not limited to, the following:  

   a. Incoming Material Inspection: All raw materials shall be inspected upon receipt to ensure compliance with Client specifications.  
   b. In-Process Inspections: Quality checks shall be conducted at each stage of the manufacturing process to ensure adherence to quality standards.  
   c. Final Product Inspection: Each batch of products shall undergo final inspection before shipment to ensure compliance with Client specifications.

**ARTICLE III: RELATIONSHIPS AND RESPONSIBILITIES**

3.1 **Manufacturer’s Responsibilities**  
The Manufacturer shall:  

   a. Employ qualified personnel to operate the Production Line, including but not limited to, Production Supervisor John Doe and QC Manager Jane Smith.  
   b. Maintain all Industrial Equipment in accordance with the Manufacturer’s Maintenance Schedule provided in Exhibit D.  
   c. Notify the Client promptly of any delays in manufacturing or quality issues.

3.2 **Client’s Responsibilities**  
The Client shall:  

   a. Provide the Manufacturer with specifications for the Products in a timely manner.  
   b. Designate a representative, Emily Brown, who shall act as the point of contact for all communications related to this Agreement.  
   c. Make timely payments as outlined in Article IV.

**ARTICLE IV: PAYMENT TERMS**

4.1 **Pricing**  
The Client agrees to pay the Manufacturer $5.00 per unit for the Products, with a minimum order quantity of 10,000 units per month.  

4.2 **Payment Schedule**  
Payments shall be made as follows:  

   a. An upfront payment of 30% of the total order value upon signing this Agreement.  
   b. The remaining 70% shall be paid within 30 days of receipt of the Products.

4.3 **Late Payments**  
Any payments not received by the due date shall incur a late fee of 1.5% per month on the outstanding balance.

**ARTICLE V: DELIVERY AND ACCEPTANCE**

5.1 **Delivery Schedule**  
The Manufacturer shall deliver the Products to the Client’s facility located at 789 Distribution St, Chicago, Illinois 60601 on or before the 15th of each month.

5.2 **Acceptance Testing**  
The Client shall conduct acceptance testing within five (5) business days of receipt of the Products. If the Products do not conform to the specifications outlined in Exhibit A, the Client shall provide written notice to the Manufacturer, and the Manufacturer shall, at its discretion, either replace or repair the Products at no additional charge.

**ARTICLE VI: WARRANTIES AND INDEMNITIES**

6.1 **Manufacturer’s Warranty**  
The Manufacturer warrants that the Products shall be free from defects in material and workmanship for a period of twelve (12) months from the date of delivery.

6.2 **Indemnification**  
The Manufacturer agrees to indemnify and hold harmless the Client, its officers, directors, and employees from any claims, damages, losses, or expenses arising out of the Manufacturer’s breach of this Agreement or negligent acts.

**ARTICLE VII: CONFIDENTIALITY**

7.1 **Confidential Information**  
Both parties agree to maintain the confidentiality of any proprietary information exchanged during the term of this Agreement, including but not limited to production methods, technical specifications, and business operations.

**ARTICLE VIII: TERM AND TERMINATION**

8.1 **Term**  
This Agreement shall commence on the date first written above and shall continue for a period of three (3) years unless terminated earlier in accordance with this Article.

8.2 **Termination for Cause**  
Either party may terminate this Agreement for cause if the other party fails to cure a material breach within thirty (30) days after receiving written notice of such breach.

**ARTICLE IX: MISCELLANEOUS**

9.1 **Governing Law**  
This Agreement shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the State of California.

9.2 **Dispute Resolution**  
Any disputes arising out of this Agreement shall be resolved by arbitration in Los Angeles, California, in accordance with the rules of the American Arbitration Association.

9.3 **Entire Agreement**  
This Agreement constitutes the entire agreement between the parties with respect to its subject matter and supersedes all prior agreements and understandings, whether written or oral.

**IN WITNESS WHEREOF**, the parties hereto have executed this Manufacturing Agreement as of the date first above written.

