**ARTICLE X: PRICING AND PAYMENT TERMS**

10.1 **Pricing Structure**  
The pricing for the Products shall be as outlined in Exhibit E. Prices are subject to change annually based on the Consumer Price Index (CPI) or other agreed-upon metrics, with a notice period of at least thirty (30) days prior to any increase.

10.2 **Payment Schedule**  
The Client shall pay the Manufacturer within thirty (30) days of receipt of the invoice for the Products delivered. Invoices shall be issued on the first business day following the delivery of each monthly shipment.

10.3 **Late Payment Penalties**  
If the Client fails to make payment within the specified time frame, a late fee of 1.5% per month shall be applied to the outstanding balance. This fee will accrue daily and will be applied until the total amount due is paid in full.

10.4 **Payment Method**  
Payments shall be made via wire transfer, automated clearing house (ACH), or check, as mutually agreed upon by both parties. Relevant banking details shall be provided by the Manufacturer at the onset of this Agreement.

**ARTICLE XI: PRODUCT RECALL AND RETRIEVAL**

11.1 **Product Recall Protocol**  
In the event that a recall of the Products is necessary due to safety concerns or non-compliance with applicable regulations, the Manufacturer shall notify the Client immediately. The Manufacturer is responsible for all costs associated with the recall process, including transportation and disposal of the recalled Products.

11.2 **Retrieval of Non-Conforming Products**  
If any Products are determined to be non-conforming and require retrieval, the Manufacturer shall coordinate with the Client to arrange for the return of such Products. The Manufacturer shall bear all costs associated with the retrieval process, including shipping and handling.

**ARTICLE XII: FORCE MAJEURE**

12.1 **Definition**  
Neither party shall be liable for any failure to perform its obligations under this Agreement if such failure results from circumstances beyond its reasonable control, including but not limited to acts of God, war, terrorism, labor disputes, or governmental actions (hereinafter referred to as "Force Majeure").

12.2 **Notice of Force Majeure**  
The affected party must provide written notice to the other party within five (5) business days of the occurrence of any Force Majeure event. Failure to provide such notice shall result in the waiver of the right to claim this excuse.

**ARTICLE XIII: ASSIGNMENT AND SUBCONTRACTING**

13.1 **Assignment**  
Neither party may assign or transfer its rights or obligations under this Agreement without the prior written consent of the other party. Any attempted assignment in violation of this clause shall be null and void.

13.2 **Subcontracting**  
The Manufacturer may subcontract portions of the production process to third-party vendors, provided that the Manufacturer remains fully responsible for the quality and timely delivery of the Products. The Manufacturer shall notify the Client in writing of any such subcontracting arrangements.

**ARTICLE XIV: HEALTH AND SAFETY COMPLIANCE**

14.1 **Compliance with Laws**  
The Manufacturer warrants that all Products delivered under this Agreement shall comply with applicable health and safety regulations and standards. The Manufacturer shall provide documentation to the Client demonstrating compliance upon request.

14.2 **Health and Safety Audits**  
The Client reserves the right to conduct health and safety audits of the Manufacturer’s facilities and processes at reasonable times during the term of this Agreement. The Manufacturer agrees to grant access to its facilities and cooperate with the Client’s audit procedures.

