**ARTICLE XV: INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY RIGHTS**

15.1 **Ownership of Intellectual Property**  
The Manufacturer and the Client agree that all intellectual property rights related to the Products, including but not limited to patents, trademarks, copyrights, and trade secrets, shall remain the property of the respective party that created or developed such intellectual property. Any modifications or enhancements made to the Products during the term of this Agreement shall be jointly owned unless otherwise agreed upon in writing.

15.2 **License Grant**  
The Manufacturer grants the Client a non-exclusive, royalty-free, and irrevocable license to use any intellectual property rights associated with the Products solely for the purpose of marketing, selling, and distributing the Products. This license shall terminate upon the expiration or termination of this Agreement.

15.3 **Confidentiality of Intellectual Property**  
Both parties agree to maintain the confidentiality of any proprietary information or trade secrets shared during the course of this Agreement. This includes any technical know-how, product designs, and business strategies. Disclosure of such information to third parties is strictly prohibited unless required by law, regulation, or with the prior written consent of the disclosing party.

**ARTICLE XVI: DISPUTE RESOLUTION**

16.1 **Negotiation**  
In the event of any dispute arising out of or relating to this Agreement, the parties shall first attempt to resolve the dispute through good faith negotiations. Each party shall designate a representative with the authority to negotiate on its behalf.

16.2 **Mediation**  
If the dispute is not resolved through negotiation within thirty (30) days, either party may initiate mediation proceedings by providing written notice to the other party. The mediation shall be conducted in accordance with the rules of a mutually agreed-upon mediation organization. The parties shall share the costs of mediation equally.

16.3 **Arbitration**  
Should mediation fail to resolve the dispute, the parties agree to submit the matter to binding arbitration in accordance with the rules of the American Arbitration Association (AAA). The arbitration shall take place in the jurisdiction where the Client is located, and the arbitrator’s decision shall be final and binding.

**ARTICLE XVII: TERMINATION**

17.1 **Termination for Cause**  
Either party may terminate this Agreement immediately upon written notice if the other party:  
(a) breaches any material term or condition of this Agreement and fails to cure such breach within thirty (30) days after receiving written notice of the breach;  
(b) becomes insolvent or files for bankruptcy; or  
(c) ceases to conduct its business in the ordinary course.

17.2 **Termination for Convenience**  
The Client may terminate this Agreement for any reason by providing the Manufacturer with thirty (30) days’ written notice. In such case, the Client shall pay for all Products delivered and accepted prior to the date of termination.

**ARTICLE XVIII: INDEMNIFICATION**

18.1 **Indemnification by Manufacturer**  
The Manufacturer agrees to indemnify, defend, and hold harmless the Client, its affiliates, and their respective officers, directors, employees, and agents from and against any claims, losses, damages, liabilities, or expenses (including reasonable attorneys' fees) arising out of or related to:  
(a) any breach of this Agreement by the Manufacturer;  
(b) the Manufacturer’s negligence or willful misconduct; or  
(c) any claims related to the Products, including but not limited to product liability claims.

18.2 **Indemnification by Client**  
The Client agrees to indemnify, defend, and hold harmless the Manufacturer, its affiliates, and their respective officers, directors, employees, and agents from and against any claims, losses, damages, liabilities, or expenses (including reasonable attorneys' fees) arising out of or related to:  
(a) any breach of this Agreement by the Client;  
(b) the Client’s negligence or willful misconduct; or  
(c) any claims related to the marketing or distribution of the Products by the Client.

